2026-06-01 16:46:30,476 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To meet the tender's GDPR compliance and security requirements, our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l., can implement the following measures based on our existing capabilities. 

Firstly, regarding data protection, we have experience with GDPR compliance, having a Data Protection Officer appointed and contactable at dpo@nexus-engineering.it. We ensure standard data residency within the EU only, which aligns with the requirement of hosting data exclusively on the territory of the European Union. Our cross-border transfer policy is to prohibit such transfers by default unless there's an explicit legal basis, further ensuring GDPR compliance.

For anonymisation and protection of sensitive data, we can utilise tools like Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. This capability ensures that any sensitive information can be appropriately encrypted or anonymised as required.

Regarding AI explainability and transparency, our ai_security_controls include output PII redaction, which means we can ensure that personally identifiable information is protected in the outputs of our AI systems. Moreover, with confidence threshold escalation, we can flag low-confidence recommendations for human review, ensuring that explanations for AI-driven suggestions are traceable and understandable.

To prevent automated decisions without explicit validation, we design our AI solutions as tools of assistance rather than autonomous decision-makers. This approach aligns with the tender's requirement that no decision should be automated without an agent's explicit validation.

Additionally, our access control standards, including multi-factor authentication (MFA) enforced through methods like TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), ensure that only authorised personnel have access to the system and data. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) design experience allows us to implement fine-grained permissions, limiting access to sensitive information on a need-to-know basis.

Our network security measures, such as Zero-trust architecture, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth strategies, protect against unauthorised access and data breaches. Regular penetration testing (at least annual, with the last test conducted on 2024-09-15) and our experience with DDoS mitigation further enhance the security posture of our proposed solution.

To address the requirement for high availability and performance, we can leverage our experience with audit and logging practices that include real-time SIEM integration. This ensures prompt detection and response to any security incidents or system downtime, maintaining the required 99.9% availability objective.

Lastly, considering environmental constraints, while specific details on low-carbon infrastructure are not provided in our context, we can focus on optimising resource usage and energy efficiency in our solution design to contribute positively to reducing the environmental footprint of the City of Belval's information systems.

In summary, by leveraging our existing security controls, GDPR compliance measures, AI explainability features, access control standards, network security practices, and performance optimization capabilities, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can propose a solution that meets the tender's requirements for strict GDPR compliance, AI transparency, and security while also considering environmental impact.
