2026-06-01 16:50:50,761 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # 1. Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., a consortium of specialized agents, proposes to design, implement, and deploy an artificial intelligence solution for the City of Belval. Our solution aims to improve the efficiency of administrative services and enhance the quality of service rendered to users. Leveraging our expertise in AI-powered document management systems, digital workplace transformations, and compliance with regulatory requirements, we will deliver a tailored solution that meets the City's specific needs.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in their daily missions, providing access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. The solution must integrate with existing systems, ensure high availability and performance, and comply with regulatory requirements such as GDPR. Additionally, the City emphasizes the importance of sovereignty, environmental sustainability, and innovation.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution will utilize the Mistral 7B Instruct Large Language Model (LLM), fine-tuned using LoRA or QLoRA methods to adapt to the client's specific domain and tone requirements. We will employ Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities to provide accurate and relevant information to agents, retrieving context-specific information from internal procedures, regulatory texts, and documents.

For integration, we will use REST, GraphQL, and SOAP APIs, as well as API gateways like Kong, to connect with the City's civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories. Our solution will be hosted on a SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale, ensuring data residency and compliance with GDPR requirements.

To ensure high availability and performance, we will implement containerization using Docker and Kubernetes, leveraging our experience with IAC tools like Terraform and Ansible. Our typical response time is 1800 ms, and we have achieved an availability of 99.92% in past projects. We will also utilize Prometheus and Grafana for monitoring and optimization.

Our security measures include implementing access control standards such as multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), role-based access control (RBAC), and network security measures like zero-trust architecture, micro-segmentation, and defense-in-depth strategies. We conduct regular penetration testing, with the last test conducted on 2024-09-15.

To address environmental constraints, we will utilize green hosting partners such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, which offer 100% renewable energy and have ISO14001 certification. Our digital sobriety practices include INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy, resulting in a typical energy reduction of 35%.

Our budget for this project is estimated based on our standard pricing model, with a target gross margin percentage of 28% and a minimum acceptable margin percentage of 18%. The total contract value is 3 million euros over 4 years, with an average annual revenue of 750,000 euros. Our standard daily rates range from 550 to 1050 euros per day, depending on the role.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements specified in the tender have been left unaddressed by our proposal. However, we note that some specific details, such as exact personnel allocation and detailed performance benchmarks for response time and availability, are not provided due to the nature of the information available from our agents.

# 5. Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is confident in its ability to deliver a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for efficiency, quality, sovereignty, sustainability, and innovation. By leveraging our expertise in AI, compliance, security, and sustainability, we are well-positioned to support the City's digital transformation strategy and improve the services provided to its users.
